      "_id": "626193ff1cfe7e5292a29294",
      "author": {
        "_id": "5acad9ecc9dba010c9c3ec68",
        "alias": "Evolutionary Vicuna",
        "aliasID": "65ba088fed6eefce4ca8dc62",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": "https://canny.io/images/a96149971e91f0ceb638e9e86cef2b08.gif",
        "created": "2018-04-09T03:11:40.225Z",
        "name": "Tupper - VRChat Head of Community",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": null
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "5b0746088fa72313783e3269",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2022-04-21T17:27:27.198Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "6261708730202f529ea6058a",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 4
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": "626193ff1cfe7e5292a29212",
      "statusChangeNewStatus": "closed",
      "value": "Hi!\nI understand why you might want this, but **we don't plan on implementing the ability to have unlimited PhysBones on Quest.** Here's why.\nPhysBones, while very performant, still hits the XR2 pretty hard given enough work to do. We try to optimize as best as possible especially for new features on Quest. This is a *brand new feature for Quest* and nothing else existed before in its place.\nHowever, we have to be very careful. Due to the extreme prevalence of Very Poor avatars on Quest, we have far less headroom on the Quest than we expect. We already exceed Meta's recommendations for various systems by a pretty big margin, and VRChat's system-level optimizations are reaching a point of diminishing returns. \nTo be extremely to-the-point: We have very significant performance problems on the Quest that we constantly push back against, and we have no interest in adding in another unlimited factor that would kill performance across the board.\nAs much as we'd like to let people do whatever they want whenever they want, we've previously observed that without any hard limits, average numbers tend to balloon way out of control without any way for us to reasonably fix the issue. \nThat's why we've implemented the limit. If it turns out that it's extremely restrictive, we can approach it again later-- however, I do not think this is likely. \nNotably, the soft-cap on DynBones on PC has been half of the PB limit for years, and most avatar authors have adapted and dropped below that line to ensure they're performant and that everyone sees their hard work. \nSince the PhysBones limits are **double** that DB limit and Quest has never had a system like this before, I expect Quest avatar authors to adapt extremely quickly, and with very little loss of fidelity.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
